<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Cleans corpse taint off apparel at stoves and the campfire. Mirrors
       vanilla's productless burn recipes (BurnApparel etc.), except the
       ingredient survives: the recipe's worker class
       (BoilTaintedGear.RecipeWorker_BoilGear) overrides the vanilla
       ingredient-consumption hook to untaint the item and charge the
       configured durability cost instead of destroying it.

       The ingredient filter is a C# subclass (ThingFilter_TaintedGear)
       because "currently tainted" is per-thing state that no def-level
       filter field can express; its base state (Apparel category) is what
       the player sees and edits in the bill dialog. -->
  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>BoilTaintedGear_BoilGear</defName>
    <workerClass>BoilTaintedGear.RecipeWorker_BoilGear</workerClass>
    <label>boil tainted gear</label>
    <description>Boil apparel that was worn by the dead in a big pot of water to wash the taint off. Slow, careful work that takes over three times as long as cooking a simple meal - and clumsy cooks are much slower still. The scrubbing wears the item out: it loses a share of its current durability (10% by default, see mod settings) but keeps its quality, color and style.</description>
    <jobString>Boiling tainted gear.</jobString>
    <!-- Work balance (RimWorld 1.6): burn apparel 60 / cremate corpse 180 /
         cook simple meal 300 / butcher creature 450, all at near-identical
         skill speed curves. Boiling saves the item instead of destroying it,
         so it costs 3.3x a meal and 16x burning, and the Cooking-2 skill
         gate keeps total novices out (same mechanism as fine/lavish meals).
         CookSpeed runs 0.4x at skill 0 to 1.6x at 20: the worst allowed cook
         (level 2) needs ~1920 ticks per item, a legendary one ~625 - hard
         labor for rookies, quick for masters. -->
    <workAmount>1000</workAmount>
    <workSpeedStat>CookSpeed</workSpeedStat>
    <requiredGiverWorkType>Cooking</requiredGiverWorkType>
    <workSkill>Cooking</workSkill>
    <skillRequirements>
      <Cooking>2</Cooking>
    </skillRequirements>
    <effectWorking>Cook</effectWorking>
    <soundWorking>Recipe_CookMeal</soundWorking>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter Class="BoilTaintedGear.ThingFilter_TaintedGear">
          <categories>
            <li>Apparel</li>
          </categories>
        </filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter>
      <categories>
        <li>Apparel</li>
      </categories>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
    <defaultIngredientFilter>
      <categories>
        <li>Apparel</li>
      </categories>
    </defaultIngredientFilter>
    <recipeUsers>
      <li>ElectricStove</li>
      <li>FueledStove</li>
      <li>Campfire</li>
    </recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
